Dear Mr Hollis,

LETTER BEFORE CLAIM

I write about the kitchen works your company carried out at 9 Elm Grove, Saltford under quotation Q-2231, which I accepted on 2 May 2023.

1. The quartz worktop cracked at the sink within two weeks of fitting. I reported this to you on 19 June 2023. You said it was a "resin line" and on 2 August refused to replace it.

2. On 3 July 2023 a badly made waste pipe joint leaked through to my living room ceiling, which has had to be propped.

3. The cooker hood was not ducted to the outside as the quotation states.

An independent chartered surveyor, Mr Martin Greaves MRICS, inspected the kitchen on 9 August 2023. His report (attached separately) confirms all three are defects in your workmanship and estimates the cost of putting them right at £3,370.

I have paid £11,580 of the £18,600 contract price. I am withholding the final invoice INV-1987 (£7,020) until the defects are fixed.

Please either confirm within 14 days of this letter, that is by 4 September 2023, that you will carry out all the remedial works at no cost within a reasonable time, or agree to reduce the final invoice by £3,370.

If I do not receive a satisfactory response by that date I intend to issue a claim in the County Court without further notice, and I will ask the court to order you to pay my costs.

Yours sincerely,

Priya Nair

